LAST_SUCCESS=Phase 2 COMPLETE + BIDIRECTIONAL verified on Pixel 2 XL (2026-05-30). war.signal (wac-plugged signal-ui+signal-engine) on the hybrid stack: in-canvas QR (run-length divs) scanned off panel -> LINKED -> connected -> phone->device receive rendered live; AND device->phone send (typed on war.ime.keyboard -> Enter -> chat::send -> arrived on phone Note-to-Self, user-confirmed). dioxus UI + Signal protocol + wasi:tls + writable /state, all through wart-host on aarch64. KEYBOARD FIX: composer needed onmousemove — dioxus-canvas only dispatches onmousedown (which calls editor_attach) for DRAGGABLE (F_MOVE) elements; without onmousemove the field focuses but the IME never attaches (caret shows, no keyboard). Phase 2 (engine + UI + on-device, both directions) DONE.
NOTES=Host change: LoadedApp::state_dir() (<install_dir>/state/) + read-write /state preopen in standalone.rs + lib.rs cold path + run_once.rs (task 38 had only RO /assets). Network/Signal-CA already host-side (task 66). In-canvas QR: signal-ui QrView run-length-merges each module row into solid divs, laid out once (link-url emitted once). qrcode crate (matrix only). signal-engine: temp eprintln link-url -> logcat for bring-up capture. GOTCHAS: adb push <dir> <existing-dir> NESTS (signal.warpkg/signal.warpkg) -> installer read stale first warpkg; rm -rf device dir before push. Host IS aot-cache-correct (loader self-heals on wasm_sha256 drift). Install needs LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/data/local/tmp. Redeploy: build host (build-host-android.sh) -> run-hybrid-stack.sh (but its EXIT trap tears down on timeout-kill; start arbiter manually if needed) -> rm -rf device warpkg + clean push + --install + arbiter launch war.signal. Rebuild app: wac plug signal_ui.wasm --plug signal_engine.wasm -o app.wasm; cp to warpkg/components/ui.wasm. FOLLOW-UPS: device->phone send test (type in composer); display-name resolution (still raw ACIs); QR-in-canvas could move to a host image primitive later. Plan: ~/.claude/plans/cat-task-state-serene-bee.md
